  "audience_note": "<b>Broad pullback vs. a strong comparable week:</b> sessions, users, and engaged sessions were all down 30&ndash;40% YoY this week (sessions −33.4%, users −37.8%, engaged sessions −33.9%) against last October's much higher baseline. Pages/session actually improved (<b>1.63</b>, +15.9% YoY) as repeat-visit share held up better than new-visitor traffic (new visitors −34.2% vs. repeat visits −28.3%), pushing the repeat-visit share to <b>50.5%</b> from 46.8% a year ago. YTD the softness is more moderate but still broad-based: sessions −14.9%, engagement rate down 5.5 pts, and session duration down 17.1% YoY, while repeat-visit share YTD still edges out last year (49.7% vs 49.0%).",
